    "body": "`/` has special treatment as a separating character in the pathname component, but not in the hash (where / has special meaning only for libraries that choose to treat it that way).\r\n\r\nAs one workaround, you can use a regex group, like so:\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst pattern = new URLPattern('/#/books/:id([^/]+)', 'http://example.com');\r\npattern.test(\"http://example.com/#/books/1/page/0\") // false\r\n```",
